// Archives written by bsdtar 3.5.3 (macOS tar) from one small site, with COPYFILE_DISABLE=1.
// The site: index.html, assets/app.js, assets/style.css, .DS_Store and a module under a
// 140-character path (ustar puts part of it in the prefix field, pax in a path record, gnutar
// in an L record). Plain tars are cut after their end-of-archive blocks (the 10 KB record
// padding is dropped); the .tgz files are byte-for-byte what `tar -czf - .` (and
// `tar -czf - dist` from the parent) wrote.
//
// Regenerate: cd site && COPYFILE_DISABLE=1 tar --format ustar -cf ../ustar.tar . (likewise
// --format pax and --format gnutar, and tar -czf for the .tgz files); symlink.tar holds
// `ln -s index.html link.html`, hardlink.tar `ln index.html copy.html`.

